<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Shifts' cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because most of its
    consumers are still in Base: DashboardService and AdminDashboardService build the
    home and admin dashboards off IShiftView and IShiftManagementServiceRead,
    AccountDeletionService cancels signups and drops volunteer profiles,
    UserParticipationBackfillService and SuspendNonCompliantMembersJob read the active
    burn, and ShiftVolunteerSearchBuilder / the Shell authorization handlers read the
    coordinator surface. A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Shifts would therefore make
    Base reference a section and cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    The split is carved from the call sites, not from the interfaces (Notifications'
    rule). IShiftManagementService has ~50 members and 73 consumer files; only the
    thirteen reads on IShiftManagementServiceRead, the six on IShiftVolunteerProfiles
    and the seven dev-fixture verbs on IShiftSeeding have a caller outside the section.
    The other ~25 — the whole rota/shift generation, coordinator-dashboard and
    post-event-stats surface — stay on the internal IShiftManagementService, which
    inherits the three leaf interfaces so the section's own call sites are unchanged.
    Same shape for IShiftSignupService: four members leave (IShiftSignups), five more
    serve only Humans.Development's dashboard seeder (IShiftSignupSeeding, Teams'
    rule — the seeder builds a multi-section fixture, so the verbs come to the leaf
    rather than the seeding going into the section), and the remaining ten stay
    internal.

    References Humans.Interfaces (IApplicationService, IInvalidator, SurfaceBudget,
    Grandfathered) and Humans.Domain — both below Humans.Application, so this cannot
    cycle. Humans.Domain is here for one reason: the section's persisted-string enums
    (SignupStatus, ShiftPeriod, ShiftPriority, RotaPeriod, BuildSubPeriod) are named by
    Base and by other sections and carry EnumStringStabilityTests rows, so they stay in
    Humans.Domain.Enums (Teams' rule).

    No entity crosses this boundary. Shift / ShiftSignup / Rota / EventSettings /
    VolunteerEventProfile are internal sealed types in Humans.Shifts.Domain, and every
    leaf member that used to return one returns a flat projection instead
    (ShiftUserSummary, UrgentShiftInfo / ShiftInfo / RotaInfo, ShiftVolunteerProfileInfo,
    BurnSettingsInfo, and Guid ids on the seeding verbs).
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Domain\Humans.Domain.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
